  "summary": "A guarded local capacity profile now drives fixed offered load through the real financial application service and a real native continuous worker. It measures hot and independent account pairs, two tenants, exact replay/rejection outcomes, authoritative reads, latency distributions, queue growth, pool/lock samples and bounded resources. Receipt storage reuses one scoped transaction for consecutive messages from the same tenant; every message retains its controlled function and Lamport checks. Publication preparation reads diagnostic origin in its existing query. Three same-source baseline calibrations and two three-run candidate cohorts retain favourable and limited results. Default batch 10 remains. Three final default runs qualify 10 offered commands per second for the stated component workload, followed by actual Redis interruption and worker process restart. A separate real signed slow TLS receiver check proves posting and lease renewal continue while HTTP waits.",
